  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "If you have no reason to believe the friend had the owner’s permission, removing tools from a storage room at night is likely theft and should be reported. First verify context safely: avoid confrontation, observe more if possible, or ask the friend calmly whether they had permission. If they did not, notify the property owner or manager and provide what you observed (time, description, photos if safe to take). If the taking is in progress or the situation seems dangerous, call the police. Preserve your safety and avoid public accusations; speaking to the friend first is an option, but if they admit wrongdoing or refuse to return items, report it."
}

