{
  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "In general you should report it. Taking company property without permission is theft and could put your own job and integrity at risk if you do nothing. Follow your employer's policy — report confidentially to your manager, HR, or through an anonymous hotline if available. That said, context matters: if it was a genuine misunderstanding (e.g., supplies your parent thought were free) you might first talk privately with your parent and encourage them to return the items, but if they refuse or the value/intent looks criminal, report it and avoid confronting them alone after hours."
}

